post_install() {
  cat <<'MSG'

steel-sandbox: global Flatpak permission overrides are now active.

  Every Flatpak application has lost home access, host access, device
  access, X11, and network. Grants are made back per-app, from nothing.

  Expect breakage, and expect it to be confusing. The usual symptoms:

    empty file dialog        the app needs a portal, or a filesystem grant
    "cannot find its data"   grant its own data directory
    no sound / no camera     grant the device explicitly
    app will not start       often fallback-x11; check with `flatpak run -v`

  To grant one permission to one app:

      flatpak override --user --filesystem=xdg-documents org.example.App

  Or use Flatseal, which is installed for exactly this purpose.

  docs/escape-hatches.md maps each symptom to the specific grant.

  These overrides apply to the SYSTEM Flatpak installation. To apply the
  same defaults to your per-user installation:

      install -Dm644 /var/lib/flatpak/overrides/global \
        ~/.local/share/flatpak/overrides/global

MSG
}

post_upgrade() {
  post_install
}

pre_remove() {
  cat <<'MSG'

steel-sandbox: removing this package restores Flatpak's default permissions.

  Applications will regain whatever their manifests requested, which for
  many popular applications includes full home directory access.

MSG
}
